; test rebase
; `x = iadd p, K` with a dominating `w = iadd p, J` on a memory base
; becomes `x = iadd w, K-J` so `p`'s post-increment uses funnel
; through `w` — the shape aarch64 post-index fusion needs.
;
; v5 (p+1 again) folds to an alias of v2: the same-offset case used to
; crash because `change_to_alias` ran on a still-attached result.
; check: v5 -> v2
; check: v7 = iadd v5, v8
; check: store v5, v0
; check-not: v5 = iadd
function %f(i64) {
block0(v0: i64):
    v1 = iconst.i64 1
    v2 = iadd.i64 v0, v1
    v3 = uload8.i32 notrap v0
    v4 = iconst.i64 1
    v5 = iadd.i64 v0, v4
    v6 = iconst.i64 3
    v7 = iadd.i64 v0, v6
    store.i64 v5, v0
    store.i64 v7, v2
    return
}
